	// Health Report whether this instance is initialized and able to serve
	//
	// Modelled on Vault's `/sys/health`: the status code carries the state so
	// a liveness or readiness probe needs no body parsing, and the body says
	// the same thing for a human.
	//
	// `200` — initialized, the database answers, and audit is disabled or at
	// least one configured target can be written. A partial audit failure
	// remains ready because requests can still be recorded.
	// `501` — reachable, but not initialized (Vault's code for the same
	// state). The console reads this to decide whether first run is the
	// wizard or the sign-in screen, WITHOUT posting to `/sys/init`, which would
	// claim the instance.
	// `503` — the database does not answer, OR audit is configured and no
	// target can be written. Either way nothing can be served: audit fails
	// closed, so an instance that cannot record a request cannot answer one
	// (duf-dya). This is a READINESS signal — a degraded instance should be
	// taken out of rotation, not restarted, because a restart cannot empty a
	// full disk.
