	// endpoint, then use the ordinary authenticated platform endpoints. There
	// is no privileged side door — that is what allows end-to-end tests to
	// bootstrap a server without a browser (ADR-0012).
	//
	// Accepted risk, documented rather than engineered around: while
	// uninitialized, whoever reaches this endpoint first owns the deployment.
	// Do not expose an uninitialized instance publicly.
	//
	// Alongside the credentials, the response carries the recovery shares
	// (ADR-0024): a sharded proof of custody for `/sys/recovery`, shown once
	// like the credentials and verified server-side against a stored digest.
	// The share count and threshold are fixed here, at initialization —
	// there is no rekey ceremony.
