// GetEncryption Read keyring state and the remembered encryption health
//
// Root-only, like the audit target list: KEK references and key versions
// are rotation bookkeeping, not something every principal needs. The
// keyring listing carries no key material — only each entry's purpose,
// version, the KEK version that wrapped it, and when that wrapping was
// produced. `state` is the same remembered heartbeat answer `/sys/health`
// reports; after rotating the KEK at the key service, entries whose
// `kek_ref` still names the old version are the rows `rewrap` exists for.
//
// Corresponds with GET /api/v1/encryption (the `GetEncryption` operationId).
