// RotateEncryption Mint a new data-key version for every keyring purpose
//
// DEK rotation (ADR-0024): a fresh key version is minted locally for
// every purpose, wrapped by the key service, and becomes what new writes
// use. Old versions stay in the keyring so existing payloads, MACs and
// audit entries verify forever — nothing is re-encrypted. Tokens signed
// with the previous key version keep verifying and age out within the
// token TTL. Audit-entry HMACs record the key version that produced
// them, so HMAC correlation of a sensitive value across the rotation
// boundary changes by design.
//
// The request body is empty. Peer replicas adopt the new versions at
// their next heartbeat; until then a payload written or token signed
// under the new version by this replica does not verify on a peer that
// has not yet refreshed. Rotate in a quiet window on multi-replica
// deployments.
