// RewrapEncryptionWithResponse Rewrap every keyring entry under the key service's current KEK
//
// The explicit follow-through a KEK rotation requires (ADR-0024): the key
// service rotates its KEK on the operator's order, and this operation —
// equally deliberate, equally attributable — rewraps the stored keyring
// rows under the new version. Payloads are never touched; the data keys
// do not change. Until it runs, keyring rows stay wrapped under the old
// KEK version, and retiring that version at the key service would leave
// the next process start unable to unwrap anything ("sealed").
//
// The request body is empty. The operation attempts the real rewrap
// rather than pre-refusing on remembered health — a failed attempt is an
// audited failure — and the stored rows change only when every entry
// rewrapped, so a partial key-service failure changes nothing.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /api/v1/encryption/rewrap (the `RewrapEncryption` operationId).
